NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2025:MPHC-JBP:25471 3 WP-19818-2025 (iii) The District Court, preferably Special Judge/POCSO, after obtaining the said medical report,
under intimation to the victim and her parents, directly refer such case and report to the nearest Registry of the High Court;
(iv) The Registry of High Court, in turn, shall register such reference as a Writ Petition under Article 226 of the Constitution, Suo Motu, and list the matter immediately before the concerned Bench having the roster, so that appropriate orders regarding termination of pregnancy can be passed by the High Court without any undue delay;
(v) If directed by the High Court that termination of pregnancy is required then, the procedure of termination of pregnancy will be carried out in the presence of the expert team of doctors.
